= Foreword

This document is the user guide for the `bookly` template. It was designed to help Typst users create beautiful documents with ease, while providing a set of features that can be used to create professional-looking books, reports, and manuals. The template is designed to be flexible and customizable, allowing users to adapt it to their specific needs.

This guide uses the full set of features provided by the template and includes practical examples.



#v(1em)
#align(right)[Mathieu Aucejo \ 2026]

= Abstract

#set text(lang: "en")
This work presents and documents the Typst template `bookly`, designed to enable Typst users to write their documents in a modern, readable, and reproducible environment. Most of the content presented in this guide follows the "code + output" principle: a Typst excerpt presents the syntax, and its result is displayed immediately in the document. This approach allows it to be considered not only as a practical user guide, but also as a demonstration of the possibilities offered by the template.

#v(1em)
*Keywords:* Typst, template, book, Cnam, reproducible scientific publishing, user guide, documentation.
